  {
   "topic": "Ratings basis",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The current, power and thermal-resistance figures assume the device on FR-4 with the smallest recommended pads. At 25 °C ambient that gives 600 mW and 200 °C/W; referred to a 25 °C solder point it gives 920 mW and 136 °C/W. Continuous drain current falls from 500 mA to 300 mA between 25 °C and 100 °C ambient."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Derating with solder point temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Allowed dissipation stays at 100 % up to a 50 °C solder point and falls in a straight line to zero at 150 °C. Allowed continuous current stays at 100 % to 25 °C, drops to about 78 % at 75 °C and 45 % at 125 °C, and reaches zero at 150 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Safe operating area",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "For single pulses at 25 °C ambient the usable area is bounded on the left by on-resistance, on top near 0.72 A, on the right by the 50 V rating, and by a line for each pulse width from DC to 1 ms."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Body diode",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "The source-drain diode carries up to 194 mA continuous and 1.2 A peak at a 25 °C solder point, with a forward drop of 1.0 V typical and 1.5 V maximum at 180 mA."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package and materials",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "SOT23 body of green molding compound rated UL 94V-0; moisture sensitivity level 1 to J-STD-020. Leads are matte tin over an annealed Alloy 42 frame, lead free, solderable to MIL-STD-202 method 208. The part weighs about 0.008 g. It is free of lead, halogen and antimony and meets RoHS (2002/95/EC, 2011/65/EU and 2015/863/EU); halogen-free means under 900 ppm bromine, under 900 ppm chlorine, under 1500 ppm of the two together and under 1000 ppm antimony compounds."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Outline",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "All body draft angles are 7°. The gauge plane sits 0.25 mm above the seating plane."
  }
 ],
